781		In the source statement of Lemma~\ref{lem:pauli-binary} in
782		\cite{Ji2020MIPStar}, the index range of the qubit factor is printed as
783		$j \in \{1, \dots, q\}$; the intended range, used above, is
784		$j \in \{1, \dots, k\}$, as the $i$-th qudit is mapped to $k$ qubits. The
785		source also quantifies over arbitrary integers $L$; the statement above
786		takes $L$ to be a natural number, including zero, and uses the usual
787		empty-product convention for the tensor powers when $L=0$.  The index
788		correction is documented in \cite{gap:qpbt_pauli-binary-factor-index}.
789	\end{remark}

